{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character","id":1554145,"title":"Everyone's least favorite VTM character?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-04T15:40:35-07:00","id":1554145,"title":"Everyone's least favorite VTM character?","content":"Besides Ur-Shurgi and Samial Haight. Whom do you think was not a good character that was added to the lore and did nothing to improve it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T18:00:19-07:00","id":1554149,"title":"","content":"Hey, I liked Samuel Haight...<br /> <br /> Tbh, I don't like any of the Revised-era &quot;Signature Characters&quot; and I ESPECIALLY despise the V5 versions of past characters and any V5 characters in general (with the exception of Arthur Caldwell, he's actually pretty cool. Gotta give props to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> for making the only V5-exclusive NPC that I actually like)<br /> <br /> Rudi is an obvious one with a fuckton of unfortunate implications, and then there's that Ventrue trans man from one of the more recent-ish V5 books who's a self-described &quot;fuckboy&quot; whose name I can't remember, but he really stood out to me and not in a good way. <br /> <br /> I'm a trans man myself, and even though I've got a frank and open-minded attitude towards sexuality, I'd never call myself a fuckboy and honestly would be creeped out by anyone who would. Maybe I'm just being too sensitive (hell, I probably am) but that one really weirded me out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T18:51:22-07:00","id":1554150,"title":"","content":"I never warmed up to Rudi in the new setting and I don't mind the Gangrel clan all that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T19:27:23-07:00","id":1554152,"title":"","content":"Critias. Pedophile Sophist. <br /> Sascha/Myka Vykos. The modern version is just ugh..<br /> Mari/Mary the Black. Her creation makes no sense.<br /> Elimelech. He falls into Ur-Shulgi territory with his write up. Just list him as a god damn 4th Generation Malkavian and stop the stupid cryptic meta shit on the stat sheets.<br /> Azif (Jerusalem by Night) 6th gen stats, 7th gen childer, 4th gen listed, no rational.<br /> <br /> Honorable mention: All the &quot;Drowned Legacies&quot; that they'll never do anything with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T20:07:07-07:00","id":1554153,"title":"","content":"I don't mind Mary The Black even though I'm not big on the Baali, bloodline and her purpose was to be the one major regret of Michael of not being able to save her in Alba and it having lasting scars on him.<br /> <br /> I agree with just list Emmlich as a 4th generation Malkavian who has nearly fallen to the beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T03:48:23-07:00","id":1554155,"title":"","content":"<b>Vasilisa</b><br /> Nights of Prophecy had so much potential, like Vasilisa and Baba Yaga (especially if you read Rage Across Russia, the Zmei, Koshchei, the First Finger, one of the Talons of the Wyrm, her Six Armies, Gutka, the Salt Queen,one of the eldest childer of Baba Yaga and the fact She was a Shaman who dearly and truly loved and wanted to heal her land and she never hurt a truly innocent person made her such an awesome multi layered character that was just snuffed out by Vasilisa)...<br /> ...and managed to screw it<br /> But Vasilisa was especially hard to swallow... she/he was stated to be over <i>twice</i> the age of Baba Yaga (who herself had around 7000 years under her belt) and even if that thing started out as a young boy, a young child who was slated for execution by his village for killing his family and several other villagers with tools, poisons, and even by leading them into the jaws of lurking predators who managed to impress such a despicable monster as Absilimilard, Nights of Prophecy managed to reduce him to into somethign even <i>less </i>than Ur-Shulgi (in another thread I wrote why I actually saw more in him than other two dimensional elders) - yet in theory he/she had so much more background and friggin 14K years behind her back to work with... <br /> And...<br /> ...nothing<br /> Literally nothing, wrose, even less than nothing<br /> Small consolidation it is hinted Baba Yaga probably realized she became too noisy and faked her own death (the old hag has Obfuscate 9 and Thaumaturgy 9 and she already fooled the Nosferatu Antediluvian when she was freshly Embraced... doing the same after seven milleniums aganist her &quot;broodmate&quot; was not totally imposibble)<br /> Her shadow still lingers and even the Garou thread carefully in Her domain...<br /> <br /> Anyhow, Vasilisa<br /> She is my least favorite vampire character just because of the sheer wasted opportunity she/he had...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T17:27:44-07:00","id":1554184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554150#post1554150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never warmed up to Rudi in the new setting and I don't mind the Gangrel clan all that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Gangrel Clan but they should've never left the Camarilla (and at my gaming table, they never did and they never will) and Rudi is just downright awful and feels like a strawman archetype that you'd see in some right-winger's attempt at mockery or parody of &quot;woke&quot; media as opposed to an actual character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T18:46:47-07:00","id":1554186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character#post1554145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides Ur-Shurgi and Samial Haight. Whom do you think was not a good character that was added to the lore and did nothing to improve it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of wish they'd make SKINNER an official module because it is by a developer and more or less redeems the character of Samuel Haight by using him in an entirely reasonable way. It also gives the player characters the option of killing him permanently or just letting him go.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi is also a guy that I think could be fine if there was a way for the player characters to do anything with him. Like in Transylvania Chronicles V or whatever, you have the option of going to a United States general's home and brainwashing him into ordering an airstrike or go seek out a magical jawbone in the Middle East that can slay him or...anything.<br /> <br /> He suffers from the problem of Divis Mal where the developers really don't want the player characters to be the stars around him. It was the opposite design philosophy of Exalted and you can guess which I favor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554149#post1554149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I liked Samuel Haight...<br /> <br /> Tbh, I don't like any of the Revised-era &quot;Signature Characters&quot; and I ESPECIALLY despise the V5 versions of past characters and any V5 characters in general (with the exception of Arthur Caldwell, he's actually pretty cool. Gotta give props to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> for making the only V5-exclusive NPC that I actually like)<br /> <br /> Rudi is an obvious one with a fuckton of unfortunate implications, and then there's that Ventrue trans man from one of the more recent-ish V5 books who's a self-described &quot;fuckboy&quot; whose name I can't remember, but he really stood out to me and not in a good way.<br /> <br /> I'm a trans man myself, and even though I've got a frank and open-minded attitude towards sexuality, I'd never call myself a fuckboy and honestly would be creeped out by anyone who would. Maybe I'm just being too sensitive (hell, I probably am) but that one really weirded me out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the very high praise!<br /> <br /> The thing about Rudi is that I actually would be interested in the guy's write-up. He's a Gangrel activist who hangs out with a dialberist nutjob in Agata Starek and the two of them successfully helped bring about the revolution in Berlin. That is a STORY. However, V5 is allergic to write-ups for characters and lore heavy NPCs so that we didn't even get an update for Victoria Ash's stats. I don't blame Paradox for this but I do wish they'd bring better focus back to the characters.<br /> <br /> If I had any characters I didn't like for V:TM?<br /> <br /> Well, that's hard because I usually think of V:TM characters as challenges rather than enemies. Even the repulsive ones can have their place. Ballard is a character that should absolutely be horrifying to anyone but the implications of what he did to his family are reasons that he might make a good villain for example. Jacob Schumpeter being a misogynist abuser means that he's very useful if you just want a one-shot game about murdering the guy.<br /> <br /> If I have a character that don't think has much value at all to my games and just makes the game less fun, then I'd have to say the Nictuku from &quot;Grandmother's House&quot; for representing the worst of game philosophy in action.<br /> <br /> She goes with you to Baba Yaga's house, kills Baba Yaga, and then kills any Nosferatu NPCs. You cannot affect the plot and are just witnesses to it. You can't talk to her, influence her, or really resist. <br /> <br /> The opposite of my game philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-05-2025, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T21:09:32-07:00","id":1554190,"title":"","content":"If there's a character that I don't really like outside of Uri Shugi is his fellow clan mate Fatima who rebels against him because his edict of only worshiping Haqim and no one else.<br /> <br /> I can understand that her devotion to her mortal faith is laudable, but you didn't have a problem of putting fellow kindred who believe in the same to final death before hand. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-06-2025, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T10:16:46-07:00","id":1554199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554190#post1554190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's a character that I don't really like outside of Uri Shugi is his fellow clan mate Fatima who rebels against him because his edict of only worshiping Haqim and no one else. I can understand that her devotion to her mortal faith is laudable, but you didn't have a problem of putting fellow kindred who believe in the same to final death before hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fatima is something of a victim of the moving goal posts of the Assamite/Banu Haqim clan in that she was meant to be a progressive character for a very reactionary group that ended up with her being now extremely unprogressive for a much less reactionary clan. Originally, she was the first female Embraced for the Assamites when they were in full &quot;crazy diablerist murder cult&quot; mode. Which was a bit of misogyny for vampires who have always been way more egalitarian than regular humanity (because if a 4th generation vampiress tells you to eat your eyeballs, you will do it).<br /> <br /> Then the Assamites became the three castes and suddenly only the Warrior Castes were a bunch of crazy murder nutters. Fatima suddenly is just a little less special as the wizards and Judges had plenty of female members. Even then, the conflict between Islam (certainly better than the Path of Blood) and the Path of Blood happened. It's just Fatima was portrayed as a holy warrior who was religiously faithful to both the Path of Blood and Islam. Ur-Shulgi decides you can either believe in God or Haqim but not both but Fatima tries to thread the needle.<br /> <br /> Which results in the Clan Novels ending with Fatma being spared by Haqim.<br /> <br /> Two problems:<br /> <br /> 1. The good people at OPP note that the whole &quot;Islam vs. Blood Gods&quot; thing is still pretty orientalist and make the split much more secular and for a variety of reasons. The Banu Haqim are now up against the regular clan versus the Web of Knives which means that Fatima is the primary female member of a psychotic murder blood cult in the regular clan versus the mainstream clan. Which now makes her an outlier in an outlier.<br /> 2. Fatima's desire to serve both God and Haqim is a moving meaningful struggle to reconcile faith with cause but is undermined by the fact that Haqim's blood cult is a murder religion against pretty much every religious tenant of Islam. So its unintentionally ridiculous. A bit like me trying to reconcile my belief in Jesus with being a practicing Sith Lord. It makes her a massive hypocrite and religious heretic akin to the Giovanni version of Catholicism. Ur shulgi isn't right about many things but trying to thread the needle here is just insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-06-2025, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T11:48:27-07:00","id":1554201,"title":"","content":"Even more insane the fact Fatima was on the Path of Blood and not some novice, a hefty 7! <br /> I always found it confusing and interesting when in 2001 Veil of Night came out withthe Ashirra they never uptad her to have Tariq el-Sama' , the Road of Heaven or Tariq el-Harb: the &quot;Road of War,&quot; the Muslim version of the Road of Chivalry.<br /> Hell even Tariq el-Umma, the &quot;Road of Community,&quot; the Muslim version of the Road of Humanity woudl have made more sense than the Road of Blood that was built on rigorous devotion to the cause of Haqim.<br /> Ur-Shulgi was right in that one to be honest...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T12:57:24-07:00","id":1554204,"title":"","content":"Most of Beckett Jyhad's Diary take on previous characters, plus all V5 (with the exception of Julia Sowinski, she was cool).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T20:02:15-07:00","id":1554213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character#post1554145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides Ur-Shurgi</div> </div> </div> </div>Take all the fun out of it, why don't you?<br /> <br /> Gonna second Vasilisa and Elimelech, since I'm blanking on most of the NPC cast right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T20:14:47-07:00","id":1554214,"title":"","content":"I'm going to make a controversial pick: Post-Lasombra Trilogy Lucita.<br /> <br /> Lucita is more or less the iconic Vampire: The Masquerade character even if she was only introduced at the beginning of Revised. She has five novels, a comic book series, and has been adapted to the LA by Night stream by the lovely Cynthia Marie. There's many modules and fan content that stars her like Lucita's Six. I love Lucita and so do many other fans as the perfect embodiment of the dark superhero world of White Wolf.<br /> <br /> However, the decision to have her join the Sabbat was one of the dumbest decisions in all of gaming. Essentially, I can't help but think that someone up high thought that the Lasombra Signature character being a Antitribu was a bad idea. So it fell to the authors to justify it in universe.<br /> And now we're stuck with it.<br /> <br /> Worse, it becomes even more ridiculous with the fact that Lucita is now the outlier. She defects to the Sabbat because she feels that the Camarilla is ignoring the threat of Gehenna as well as a spiritual void in her soul.<br /> <br /> And in 5th Edition:<br /> <br /> 1. The Sabbat are now mindless blood horrors with no real spiritualism.<br /> 2. The Camarilla now believe in the Antediluvians.<br /> 3. The Lasombrra have defected because they understand the Gehenna Wars are full of morons.<br /> 4. White Wolf's owners know the Lasombra are awesome and everyone loves them in the LARPs as well as games like Shadows of New York.<br /> <br /> So Lucita is either dead at Talley's hand or head of a bunch of cultists in Madrid doing nothing.<br /> <br /> Oof.<br /> <br /> I'm not even sure her defection even makes sense anymore since the primary reason for her spiritual collapse was Anatole dying (combined with killing Moncada) and he's supposedly alive again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T21:01:35-07:00","id":1554215,"title":"","content":"They thought they were fixing Luciata in that clan novel trilogy and all it did was muddy the waters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-06T23:20:52-07:00","id":1554218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554215#post1554215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They thought they were fixing Luciata in that clan novel trilogy and all it did was muddy the waters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they made her more generic and then her old self became the archetypal Lasombra for 5th Edition players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-07T09:09:15-07:00","id":1554224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554214#post1554214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to make a controversial pick: Post-Lasombra Trilogy Lucita.<br /> <br /> Lucita is more or less the iconic Vampire: The Masquerade character even if she was only introduced at the beginning of Revised. She has five novels, a comic book series, and has been adapted to the LA by Night stream by the lovely Cynthia Marie. There's many modules and fan content that stars her like Lucita's Six. I love Lucita and so do many other fans as the perfect embodiment of the dark superhero world of White Wolf.<br /> <br /> However, the decision to have her join the Sabbat was one of the dumbest decisions in all of gaming. Essentially, I can't help but think that someone up high thought that the Lasombra Signature character being a Antitribu was a bad idea. So it fell to the authors to justify it in universe.<br /> And now we're stuck with it.<br /> <br /> Worse, it becomes even more ridiculous with the fact that Lucita is now the outlier. She defects to the Sabbat because she feels that the Camarilla is ignoring the threat of Gehenna as well as a spiritual void in her soul.<br /> <br /> And in 5th Edition:<br /> <br /> 1. The Sabbat are now mindless blood horrors with no real spiritualism.<br /> 2. The Camarilla now believe in the Antediluvians.<br /> 3. The Lasombrra have defected because they understand the Gehenna Wars are full of morons.<br /> 4. White Wolf's owners know the Lasombra are awesome and everyone loves them in the LARPs as well as games like Shadows of New York.<br /> <br /> So Lucita is either dead at Talley's hand or head of a bunch of cultists in Madrid doing nothing.<br /> <br /> Oof.<br /> <br /> I'm not even sure her defection even makes sense anymore since the primary reason for her spiritual collapse was Anatole dying (combined with killing Moncada) and he's supposedly alive again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically she was introduced in Vampire the Dark Ages, though her trademark was on Transylvania Chronicles I. That was the main issue while white-wolf was on trial over Underworld's Selene with Sony.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-08T13:06:46-07:00","id":1554242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554149#post1554149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rudi is an obvious one with a fuckton of unfortunate implications, and then there's that Ventrue trans man from one of the more recent-ish V5 books who's a self-described &quot;fuckboy&quot; whose name I can't remember, but he really stood out to me and not in a good way.<br /> <br /> I'm a trans man myself, and even though I've got a frank and open-minded attitude towards sexuality, I'd never call myself a fuckboy and honestly would be creeped out by anyone who would. Maybe I'm just being too sensitive (hell, I probably am) but that one really weirded me out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason lgbt people are always depicted as sex maniacs in media. As a bi myself I feel bad for the hetero sex maniacs.<br /> I initially thought rudi was a clever joke about people like me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-08T14:01:06-07:00","id":1554243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554242#post1554242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason lgbt people are always depicted as sex maniacs in media. As a bi myself I feel bad for the hetero sex maniacs.<br /> I initially thought rudi was a clever joke about people like me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the issue is Rudi never got a write up ala Children of the Inquisition or such. We've only got second hand mentions of the guy so any nuances to the character are lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-08T16:57:23-07:00","id":1554245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554242#post1554242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason lgbt people are always depicted as sex maniacs in media. As a bi myself I feel bad for the hetero sex maniacs.<br /> I initially thought rudi was a clever joke about people like me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I actually AM an LGBT sex maniac (a bisexual trans man, to be specific) and proud of it and even I was put off by Rudi. The whole Islam angle they had with him also was very off-putting, feeling less like representation and more like fetishization. Like I said, Rudi comes off more like a strawman than an actual character.<br /> <br /> Even then, that Ventrue trans man who's a self-described &quot;fuckboy&quot; is even more creepy to me. It feels like some weird Tumblr girl who's secretly a chaser for trans men (and in denial about it) wrote him.<br /> <br /> <b>Side Note:</b> As a trans person, I honestly am not <i>that </i>bothered by chasers...if they're up front and honest about it from the get-go. From my own personal experiences, the chasers who are willing to admit it right away also tend to be more respectful of boundaries while the ones who deny it and are super-insistent about being &quot;good trans allies&quot; and act all hyper-political are far more aggressive and creepy behind closed doors. As always, this is just my own experience and I do NOT speak for all trans people when it comes to this rather sensitive issue. YMMV as always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 10-08-2025, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T05:56:03-07:00","id":1554257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554245#post1554245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I actually AM an LGBT sex maniac (a bisexual trans man, to be specific) and proud of it and even I was put off by Rudi. The whole Islam angle they had with him also was very off-putting, feeling less like representation and more like fetishization. Like I said, Rudi comes off more like a strawman than an actual character.<br /> <br /> Even then, that Ventrue trans man who's a self-described &quot;fuckboy&quot; is even more creepy to me. It feels like some weird Tumblr girl who's secretly a chaser for trans men (and in denial about it) wrote him.<br /> <br /> <b>Side Note:</b> As a trans person, I honestly am not <i>that </i>bothered by chasers...if they're up front and honest about it from the get-go. From my own personal experiences, the chasers who are willing to admit it right away also tend to be more respectful of boundaries while the ones who deny it and are super-insistent about being &quot;good trans allies&quot; and act all hyper-political are far more aggressive and creepy behind closed doors. As always, this is just my own experience and I do NOT speak for all trans people when it comes to this rather sensitive issue. YMMV as always.</div> </div> </div> </div>Props for a nuanced discussion of the matter. <br /> <br /> After all, vampires have a long history of also being used to examine sexuality, gender, and queer identity in a subversive lens.<br /> <br /> Thanks for sharing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T06:08:26-07:00","id":1554258,"title":"","content":"Another couple of characters I have an issue with:<br /> <br /> <b>Khalil Ravana</b>: I think someone thought it'd be fun to have the Ravnos signature character be fun critique of the fact that everyone assumed the Clan was full of bad stereotypes by...making a character who is every awful stereotype combined. Khalil is a diablerist, liar, thief, and repulsive piece of crap without any real redeeming qualities. His sheer lack of virtues does make him stand out in the Clan Novels but not in a good way.<br /> <br /> Basically, Hesha is a priest of pure darkness and Vykos is a diabolical mastermind while Khalil is the kind of player character who pulls out a shotgun to blow up an Elder then rob their house during a quest giving session. There were some interesting ideas with the guy like him being possessed by Hazimel as well as the genuinely funny joke he did with Ramona. &quot;Hey, don't you disrespect Romani. They're not a bunch of thieves and murderers. I AM but that's just me. Really, I'm a genuine disgrace to my family.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Evil Saulot</b>: I think someone really thought revealing Saulot was an evil mastermind was one of the coolest ideas ever and never realized that it wasn't nearly as interesting as they thought. &quot;Okay, he's a bastard. Now how does that make him different from any other Antediluvian?&quot; I also felt that it was revealed in a way that I think didn't really do the necessary legwork. Revealing him as the guy who created the Baali was supposed to be, &quot;Oh, he made the worst of the worst!&quot; Except V:TM Cainite lore is based on the premise that God punished Caine by turning them into undead. You could easily read Saulot punishing the Baali founders by making them 4th generation and then going, &quot;Oh shit. That was a bad idea.&quot; Arguably, it's way more interesting.<br /> <br /> There are worse ideas, like making the Inner Circle of the Third Reich into vampires, but I think we've all collectively agreed they're so stupid they don't count. The worst element of them really was that they got all of Berlin by Night discounted rather than going, &quot;Some disgusting punks with Vicissitude pretended to be Nazis. Eventually, Rudi and company took care of them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-09-2025, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T09:01:34-07:00","id":1554264,"title":"","content":"I actually thought Rudi was a brand new character for the series. I didn't know that he appeared in earlier editions and here I thought I was getting to know the lore way better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T10:03:19-07:00","id":1554267,"title":"","content":"Vasilisa is my top least-favorite but there is one that really came a close second<br /> <b>Rasputin</b><br /> Not Vidal Jarbeaux's alias, the Fox was a nice fleshed out character<br /> But Rasputin...<br /> They never managed to nail him down and decide on one version<br /> A Malkavian (Clanbook: Malkavian)?<br /> A Follower of Set? (Clanbook: Setites)<br /> A Ventrue? (Clanbook: Ventrue)<br /> A Nosferatu (Berlin by Night)?<br /> He is/was a Shadow Lord? (ribebook: Shadow Lords, Tribebook: Silver Fangs)<br /> A Puppeteer Wraith (Guildbook: Pardoners and Puppeteers)?<br /> A Mage of the Cult of Ecstasy? (Cult of Ecstasy Tradition Book)<br /> Was even a vampire? One? Dozens? He was also three mages, four ghouls and many, many mortals....<br /> <br /> He is the worse macguffin youcan think of","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T12:25:34-07:00","id":1554270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554258#post1554258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are worse ideas, like making the Inner Circle of the Third Reich into vampires, but I think we've all collectively agreed they're so stupid they don't count. The worst element of them really was that they got all of Berlin by Night discounted rather than going, &quot;Some disgusting punks with Vicissitude pretended to be Nazis. Eventually, Rudi and company took care of them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Controversial opinion but I wasn't that upset by it since IIRC, it IS stated in Berlin By Night that Heinrich Himmler was embraced shortly after WWII had ended, right around the time he killed himself IRL, so it's pretty obvious that all of his heinous crimes against humanity were committed while he was still an ordinary mortal human and I could easily see an edgy Tremere Antitribbu dipshit wanting to embrace a notorious war criminal who was known for having an unhealthy obsession with the occult.<br /> <br /> I actually like Berlin By Night precisely because it's peak 2nd Edition &quot;Supers With Fangs&quot; gonzo badwrongfun (as I prefer that style of play and I despise personal horror) and at my games, it's still canon. Plus it gives the players at my table chance to get Heinrich Himmler and make him pay.<br /> <br /> There was really no need to officially de-canonize Berlin By Night since even with it being canon, the whole point of &quot;The Holocaust and all other crimes committed by the Nazis were entirely the fault of mortal humans with no supernatural involvement&quot; angle mentioned in Charnel Houses of Europe would still be true even with Berlin By Night being kept fully canon, since Himmler didn't become a vampire until after he had already committed all those vile acts and the Nazi regime had already collapsed.<br /> <br /> I also suspect the metaplot killing off the Tremere Antitribbu was also related to Himmler and I'm sure I'm not the only one who suspects that since I think I remember reading an old post from Baroness Nerak mentioning that on RPG.net from way back in the day.<br /> <br /> That aside, I agree with you on Evil Saulot being a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 10-09-2025, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T17:08:30-07:00","id":1554279,"title":"","content":"I can picture my Malkavian asking Saulot if he was having a bad night when he decided to make the Baali. But that would violate on how much he is starting to learn about his own clan and the others after a century and half plus of unlife.<br /> <br /> By his own admission he is not sure if they exist and to his knowledge he hasn't encountered a member of the Salburi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T18:11:43-07:00","id":1554282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554258#post1554258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another couple of characters I have an issue with:<br /> <br /> <b>Khalil Ravana</b>: I think someone thought it'd be fun to have the Ravnos signature character be fun critique of the fact that everyone assumed the Clan was full of bad stereotypes by...making a character who is every awful stereotype combined. Khalil is a diablerist, liar, thief, and repulsive piece of crap without any real redeeming qualities. His sheer lack of virtues does make him stand out in the Clan Novels but not in a good way.<br /> <br /> Basically, Hesha is a priest of pure darkness and Vykos is a diabolical mastermind while Khalil is the kind of player character who pulls out a shotgun to blow up an Elder then rob their house during a quest giving session. There were some interesting ideas with the guy like him being possessed by Hazimel as well as the genuinely funny joke he did with Ramona. &quot;Hey, don't you disrespect Romani. They're not a bunch of thieves and murderers. I AM but that's just me. Really, I'm a genuine disgrace to my family.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Evil Saulot</b>: I think someone really thought revealing Saulot was an evil mastermind was one of the coolest ideas ever and never realized that it wasn't nearly as interesting as they thought. &quot;Okay, he's a bastard. Now how does that make him different from any other Antediluvian?&quot; I also felt that it was revealed in a way that I think didn't really do the necessary legwork. Revealing him as the guy who created the Baali was supposed to be, &quot;Oh, he made the worst of the worst!&quot; Except V:TM Cainite lore is based on the premise that God punished Caine by turning them into undead. You could easily read Saulot punishing the Baali founders by making them 4th generation and then going, &quot;Oh shit. That was a bad idea.&quot; Arguably, it's way more interesting.<br /> <br /> There are worse ideas, like making the Inner Circle of the Third Reich into vampires, but I think we've all collectively agreed they're so stupid they don't count. The worst element of them really was that they got all of Berlin by Night discounted rather than going, &quot;Some disgusting punks with Vicissitude pretended to be Nazis. Eventually, Rudi and company took care of them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of Saulot creating he Baali makes sense after understanding, playing and STing Kindred of the East. The game has that setting in which it gives closure as to how definited is reality really working in WoD (depending on POV of course). The thing is the game naver had much popularity, therefore the Saiulot/Zaolat thing never got that much comprehensive background..Playing and really enjoying KotE makes me like and be able to use the idea, a very rare thing back in the day and even more so nowadays.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T21:58:29-07:00","id":1554286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554282#post1554282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea of Saulot creating he Baali makes sense after understanding, playing and STing Kindred of the East. The game has that setting in which it gives closure as to how definited is reality really working in WoD (depending on POV of course). The thing is the game naver had much popularity, therefore the Saiulot/Zaolat thing never got that much comprehensive background..Playing and really enjoying KotE makes me like and be able to use the idea, a very rare thing back in the day and even more so nowadays.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>My main issue with the Kuei Jin was how it intruded on Saulot to be honest. They made a clan of Enlightenment seekers into Interlopers and Golconda into a lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-11T01:39:07-07:00","id":1554299,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554258#post1554258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Evil Saulot</b>: I think someone really thought revealing Saulot was an evil mastermind was one of the coolest ideas ever and never realized that it wasn't nearly as interesting as they thought. &quot;Okay, he's a bastard. Now how does that make him different from any other Antediluvian?&quot; I also felt that it was revealed in a way that I think didn't really do the necessary legwork. Revealing him as the guy who created the Baali was supposed to be, &quot;Oh, he made the worst of the worst!&quot; Except V:TM Cainite lore is based on the premise that God punished Caine by turning them into undead. You could easily read Saulot punishing the Baali founders by making them 4th generation and then going, &quot;Oh shit. That was a bad idea.&quot; Arguably, it's way more interesting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah i thought evil Saulot was dull, its an issue a lot of the 3rd gen had were they're too mighty to topple and are all pretty 1 dimensional jerks. Its why I had several of them as actually dead/incapacitated or that they were working for agendas so far beyond the jihad.<br /> <br /> With the Baali I had the secret that they had an antiduelivian founder who Saulot, Haqim, Set and Cappadocious slew early on. The Baali lied for a number of reasons and forgot their history.<br /> With saulot I had his actions focused on anti infernal stuff mixed with the occasional tactical error. For example tremere and his clan was supposed to be easy to control but wasn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-11-2025, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-11T03:01:32-07:00","id":1554300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554299#post1554299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With saulot I had his actions focused on anti infernal stuff mixed with the occasional tactical error. For example tremere and his clan was supposed to be easy to control but wasn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the appeal of that<br /> <br /> Also, originally Tremere - as Mark Rein-Hagen's personal character in the first games of Ars Magica, not a surprise - always had this weird plot armour and managed to battle Saulot, who had a solid ~10K years behind his back for mental dominance...<br /> It was weird to say the least...<br /> ...but they sold it as Saulot slight miscalulation and Temere's superawesomecool mental powers<br /> <br /> V20 on the other hand approached from a different, in that Goratrix was already claimed during the <i>Dark Ages</i> that he was, in fact, Tremre having been forced outside his body after he was possessed by Saulot and that the thing that the Clan served is Saulot either struggling with the Eldest, who gain acces t othe body thanks to the Vicissitude &quot;infection&quot; or Saulot already dual mind, and Saulot the &quot;Noble&quot; /Hun battled with Saulot the Evil /P'o/Beast untill they split phisically and one part &quot;Good Saulot&quot; wandered away and Evil Saulot remained behind as the White Worm of Vienna (to be fair, not a feat, considering the level 2 power of the Cultivation Discipline called Cleave the Demon allows theKuei-jin separates his P'o from his Hun, leaving the other part of the soul in spirit form... from that materialze the other part is not that hard or find a body...)<br /> In this case, Saulot would have overtaken Tremere <i>immediately</i> - something that make more sense - and would be the force that sent Clan Tremere against the Salubri, joined the Camarilla, and would have defeated Tremere when he destroyed the Tremere antitribu.<br /> \u200b<br /> Retrospect, the whole Evils Saulot thing - even without the whole Zao-lat, the stolen Chi'iu Muh Discipline refined in to Valeren and the predmodialWay of Ten Thousand Screams he tried to walk - strangely made sense in the 2nd and revised editions hints left and right and peaked in V20<br /> The followers of Set put every Clan udner a constellation and the Salubri were under Gemini, because of their and their foudners dual nature<br /> The Assamite clanbook spoke about Haqim never trusting Saulot and his manipulations<br /> The whole Stars Above/Roots below, Kupala, fanning the feud between Absimiliard and Arikel...<br /> It was scattered in several books and editions, sometimes bleeding over other game lines, but Saulot's story suddenly made sense and the whole Ivory tablets in the Transylvania Chronicles...<br /> <br /> But for such a classical &quot;ends justify the means&quot; Machiavellian manipulator - regardless if he had good intentions or not - I tend to use what you wrote, and give him a <i>f</i><i>atal falw </i>- the ability to misscalculate things and actually able to make errors<br /> It makes him more relatable - if you can say anything like that in the case of such an ancient creture<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-11T07:57:30-07:00","id":1554302,"title":"","content":"Yeah my idea for Saulot is basically as follows.<br /> As an human Saulot is from the ancient tribes of Israel and is so old he's effectively an Henotheist rather than a montheist as an priest of the cult of Yaweh.Following his embrace He initially flirted with Monotheism with the confirmation of Caine and Abel but slowly slid back into Henotheism as he grew more aware of supplementary spiritual presences on earth. He ultimately perceives most alternative 'Gods' as either evil or simply unworthy of worship and see's most of them as a threat to humanity and good. This resulted in him neglecting his spiritual duties to his self and failing golconda as he concluded it was more important to destroy evil and protect the world than cultivate his own spiritual enlightenment-this divide within him is represented by the emergence of the Warrior, watchers and the healer Salubri as his contradictory agenda's are reflected in clan identity.<br /> <br /> in his defense of the world against evil he's had mixed result, successfully working with the other clans to end the Baali threat but also souring relations with the Kuei-jin due to a number of diplomatic gaffes. as the corruption and the depravity of the clans became more apparent he increasingly soured on the other third generation and undermines the most evil of them when he can. He is actively also working to prevent gehenna and is directly responsible for the eldests' first death. some of the strategic blunders of the nastier 3rd gen are due to not realizing Saulot's errors. Notably Lasombra with his failed attempt at apotheosis via obternerbration <br /> <br /> The diablerie of Tremere was a massive fuck up as he initially planned to integrate the Tremere as a magus arm of the Clan Salubri to help exterminate the fiends as well as gain incredibly levels of magical insight. unfortunately Tremere was no patsy and by the time he'd managed to wrestle control of Tremere's body Clan Salubri had been exterminated and he'd lost centuries of time. A massive disaster for his long term plans on a number of fronts and is now scrambling to catch up as the sheer scale of spiritual threats in the 21st century is alarming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-11-2025, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T00:22:39-07:00","id":1554309,"title":"","content":"<br /> Pretty cool idea!<br /> When I want to wander away from the more-or-less canon or &quot;inteded&quot; metaplot, usually I will go with the Followers of Set interpretation<br /> In those cases the Salubri fall within the domain of Gemini and their Progenitor was Lady Bastet.<br /> Bastet was the daughter of Ra, born from Ra's strong gaze. She was the goddes of joy, pleasure, music, and dance (hence the Salubri's powers related to songs, like Song of Reyzeel) and protection; She protected homes from evil spirits, disease, and pests like rodents and snakes (explaining the warding and healing powers of Valeren) Her domain was also the Fertility and domesticity: Her connection to fertility was strong, and she was associated with women, children, childbirth, and the home (again healing powers of Valeren and the care the Salubri gave, like a mother), She also was know as the &quot;Eye of Ra,&quot; (on of many) a powerful, protective force<br /> However... Bastet had a darker aspect; as one of the &quot;Eye of Ra&quot;, she was not only a a powerful, protective force but sometimes destructive force sent by the sun god to take vengeance on his enemies. When she was called upon to fight in vengeance she was Sekhmet, the fierce lioness goddess of war, goddess of destruction, vengeance, healing and plagues who once almost destroyed Humanity. (explaining the Warrior's Valeren powers)<br /> When Ra commanded her to go and wreak havoc upon humanity for their failure to uphold Ma'at. She did as instructed and began a horrible slaughter, killing almost everything in her sight. When Ra looked down upon the Earth, he was horrified upon seeing the carnage Sekhmet had caused and ordered her to stop and cease her rampage. However, Sekhmet, who had become overcome with bloodlust, refused and continued her rampage. Desperate to stop Sekhmet, Ra assembled the other gods and together they devised a trick: they took several jars of wine and mixed it with red pomegranate juice (which stained the wine blood red), whereupon they poured the mixture onto Sekhmet's path. Sekhmet, believing the mixture to be blood, gorged herself on it and became drunk, passing out soon after. (In this &quot;Saulot&quot; aka Bastet/Sekhmet rampaged and sired even the Baali as a tool to help to destroy the world - untill she was calmed down)<br /> <br /> In this version Saulot was female, had an affinity for felines and after coming to her senses a very remorsefull &quot;goddess&quot; who knew she almost wiped out Humanity - the Kine and foodsource of the other vampires, thus finally managed to explain why the other clans &quot;hated&quot; the noble and protetive Salubri and eagerly threw them udner the bus when opportunity arised... they never forget their progenitor almost caused the extinction of their whole race and every Salubri carried in themselves this dual nature<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-12-2025, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-14T09:32:11-07:00","id":1554362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554149#post1554149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm a trans man myself, and even though I've got a frank and open-minded attitude towards sexuality, I'd never call myself a fuckboy and honestly would be creeped out by anyone who would. Maybe I'm just being too sensitive (hell, I probably am) but that one really weirded me out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The memories....<br /> <br /> Me, reading Montreal by Night as an angry young homosexual in 1997: &quot;Queens of Mercy? A queer Sabbat coven?! LETS FUCKIN' GOOOOOO!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> Me, Finding out the Queens of Mercy were (1) a gigolo/fuccboi (2) GAY MEANS AIDS AND AIDS MEANS TRAGEDY THIS IS VERY EDGY AND COOL AND DID I MENTION IT IS THE 90s and (3) abused teen sex-worker with vicissitude pregnancy: &quot;What the hell, guys?!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6350-marcusvitel","name":"MarcusVitel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-14T18:39:56-07:00","id":1554369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcusVitel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554362#post1554362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The memories....<br /> <br /> Me, reading Montreal by Night as an angry young homosexual in 1997: &quot;Queens of Mercy? A queer Sabbat coven?! LETS FUCKIN' GOOOOOO!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> Me, Finding out the Queens of Mercy were (1) a gigolo/fuccboi (2) GAY MEANS AIDS AND AIDS MEANS TRAGEDY THIS IS VERY EDGY AND COOL AND DID I MENTION IT IS THE 90s and (3) abused teen sex-worker with vicissitude pregnancy: &quot;What the hell, guys?!&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable, though IMHO, The Queens of Mercy honestly don't bother me nearly as much as the Ventrue transman fuckboy for several reasons though.<br /> <br /> 1. They're a Sabbat coven, with all the fucked up insanity that entails<br /> <br /> 2. This is 90's era White Wolf AND it's a Black Dog book to boot. At this point, you might as well go in with the mindset of &quot;Caveat Emptor&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. Related to the second point, while the Queens of Mercy are a product of 1990s-era OG White Wolf, the Ventrue fuckboy is a product of 2020s-era Parawolf. And Parawolf is all about removing anything that may be remotely be seen as edgy or &quot;problematic&quot; to the point they outright declare groups like the Sabbat and Get of Fenris to be non-playable badwrongfun.<br /> <br /> With White Wolf in 1997, the Queens of Mercy isn't too out of line for a Black Dog release, while for Parawolf in 2024, the Ventrue trans fuckboy in Blood-Stained Love reeks of hypocrisy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-14T21:37:22-07:00","id":1554370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554369#post1554369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With White Wolf in 1997, the Queens of Mercy isn't too out of line for a Black Dog release, while for Parawolf in 2024, the Ventrue trans fuckboy in Blood-Stained Love reeks of hypocrisy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I had no problem with that character though I am neither trans nor ****able. :rimshot:<br /> <br /> The interpretation I took for the character was that he was essentially the Toreador version of a Tzimisce and an example of what OPP had already experimented with, &quot;What if we used Vicissitude for reasons OTHER than horror at the prospect of body modification?&quot;* You know, something that even my sixteen year old self noted was probably a better use of a vampire's fleshcrafting powers other than turning yourself into an Giger-monster or the not so subtly transphobic way that Vykos was always presented outside of Beckett's Jyhad Diaries.<br /> <br /> (I like Beckett's take on Vykos being, &quot;I am a horrifying murderer and supervillain mad scientist but that has nothing to do with my being trans and nonbinary. Also, the worst of it was the Dracon.&quot;)<br /> <br /> The presentation of the character basically seemed to be, &quot;I am a Tzimisce and I used Vicissitude to become ungodly beautiful and probably perfect for the Nephilim Blood Cult.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's something OPP of course got to do first with Erzulie in CBN.<br /> <br /> * We still haven't gotten a Tzimisce doctor. You know, one who actually heals but I suppose that's extra difficult even when well fed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-15T00:11:58-07:00","id":1554372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554370#post1554370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * We still haven't gotten a Tzimisce doctor. You know, one who actually heals but I suppose that's extra difficult even when well fed.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Vermundo de Sancha</b><br /> Child of <b>Efra\u00edn Sortano</b><br /> Child of <b>Fyodor Andreyev </b>(originally he is form Eastern Europe, likely from Russia - the Genealogy stops here sadly)<br /> <br /> A 10th Generation Tzimisce from Mexico City by Night<br /> While he is on the Path of Death and the Soul De Sancha is very dedicated to his duties as a doctor. People that enter his lab willingly can expect to leave healthy and whole, since the doctor thinks of them as patients that are his wards under the Hippocratic Oath. He frowns upon the excessive alterations that some of his clan members undertake, preferring to present himself without any fleshcrafted features. Along with his sire, he hosts the Universidad de Noche, a forum for scientific interested vampires that accepts guest hearers.<br /> <br /> I think this is the closest we got \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T10:46:28-07:00","id":1554525,"title":"","content":"Marcus Vitel - his pin, his thaumaturgy, he is a crappily written character<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T17:32:00-07:00","id":1554533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554525#p