</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T11:14:24-07:00","id":1554558,"title":"","content":"Vykos of the Tizsmce clan is someone I never warmed up to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-23-2025, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T11:57:25-07:00","id":1554559,"title":"","content":"Is there any others who felt the same way about Vykos?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-23-2025, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T17:44:14-07:00","id":1554624,"title":"","content":"Me. Maybe it's because I wasn't into the whole Dark Ages thing, but I felt so much word count was wasted on an edgelord whose actions only made sense to me as the result of poor impulse control rather than some grand and profound vision of what vampires should be. (Even though his Revised edition cover portrait by John Van Fleet might be my favorite bit of VtM art.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T19:54:27-07:00","id":1554633,"title":"","content":"I don't like Vykos, either.<br /> <br /> Same thing, it's just a childish edgelord with poor impulse control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T19:59:49-07:00","id":1554634,"title":"","content":"The only Vykos I considered interesting was the one who was apparently wholly different after the Dracon's seed was removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T05:18:12-07:00","id":1554638,"title":"","content":"To be honest I never understood the hype surrounding Vykos<br /> DA Vykos as CTPhipps said was somewhat interesting and I really would love to see a more fleshed out blood feud between the line of Dracon and line of Triglav Vykos found himself in the middle...<br /> But after that?<br /> Yeah she just became a bland character focuses so much on being freakish that there's not really much character left in it to explore, just the obsession with the Book of Nod for some reason - we never really got a reason why Vykos is so locked on the Book of Nod<br /> And why and how Vykos managed to land on the Path of Death and the Soul with his Mage/transhumanism background is another mystery (and as a side note Vykos never really behaved like someone who was on that weird path...)<br /> <br /> In my humble oppinion Beckett's Jyhad Diary gave him more personality than he ever had<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call my feelings a hate per see, more like a morose annoyance, a bit like with Vasilisa they could have really make Vykos something interesting, a window mayhaps you could understand the Clan as a whole, yet we got this... thing that is aaaaalieeeeeen and freakish","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-24-2025, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T08:05:04-07:00","id":1554641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554638#post1554638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest I never understood the hype surrounding Vykos<br /> DA Vykos as CTPhipps said was somewhat interesting and I really would love to see a more fleshed out blood feud between the line of Dracon and line of Triglav Vykos found himself in the middle...<br /> But after that?<br /> Yeah she just became a bland character focuses so much on being freakish that there's not really much character left in it to explore, just the obsession with the Book of Nod for some reason - we never really got a reason why Vykos is so locked on the Book of Nod<br /> And why and how Vykos managed to land on the Path of Death and the Soul with his Mage/transhumanism background is another mystery (and as a side note Vykos never really behaved like someone who was on that weird path...)<br /> <br /> In my humble oppinion Beckett's Jyhad Diary gave him more personality than he ever had<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call my feelings a hate per see, more like a morose annoyance, a bit like with Vasilisa they could have really make Vykos something interesting, a window mayhaps you could understand the Clan as a whole, yet we got this... thing that is aaaaalieeeeeen and freakish</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> But I think the Path of Death and Soul thing is purely leftover from the fact that the Path of Metamorphosis didn't exist yet and they didn't want to retcon them having otherwise.<br /> <br /> POD&amp;S was previously the Mad Scientist Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T08:15:41-07:00","id":1554642,"title":"","content":"This is where I potentially bring up a controverisal element of my dislike generally for characters that are &quot;these are shock value characters that exist for you to murder them.&quot; Which is something there's only a few of them in the game and OPP really disliked (I'm guessing) because they always get either killed off or heavily changed.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to judge that decision but also give up some thought.Also, how the idea of adding &quot;shock value&quot; elements ruins characters that might otherwise be a useful NPC. Shock can be good but...rarely is.<br /> <br /> Velya the Vivisectionist has a concept. What with fusing the Wight Little Girl to his back and the two of them existing as one. It takes an 800 year old Sabbat scholar and founder and just makes them so damned WEIRD that the only thing to do with them is put them down. It also highlights the Sabbat is full of gross nuts.<br /> <br /> Jacob Schumpeter is a Ventrue who can only feed on battered women. It's &quot;justified&quot; in so much as it actually makes sense for his character as a small insignificant Lifetime movie villain that is his concept. You CAN use Jacob intelligently and he is a &quot;cheap heat&quot; villain for a game (with the caveat that killing him will result in them having killed one of the Prince's brood)<br /> <br /> But he's an uninteresting monster too and it's notable that he got Second Inquisitioned while Bobby Weatherbottom ended up putting his girlfriend into a coma and feeding her blood constantly so he can feed on her (I had her as a Thin Blood so she could be an eternally regenerating blood bag). Bobby is objectively worse than Jacob in many ways but the shock value feels consistent while the other is, &quot;bad man.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then there's good characters ruined by shock value. Horatio Ballard being a pedophile Ventrue sort of drowns out all elements of his character even if it's only him feeding on children of his family versus anything worse (I'm not getting into that). That's solely so the players can justify killing him and making him the villain in any fight for Prince.<br /> <br /> Then there's Jan Pieterszoon.<br /> <br /> Yeah, we know why he died at Prague. But also we have no idea how his feeding restriction related to his past and probably any attempt to explore that would only made it worse. It was something I played with in my rejected Theo Bell novel pitch but I couldn't thread that needle and ditched it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T12:32:17-07:00","id":1554645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554642#post1554642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Velya the Vivisectionist has a concept. What with fusing the Wight Little Girl to his back and the two of them existing as one. It takes an 800 year old Sabbat scholar and founder and just makes them so damned WEIRD that the only thing to do with them is put them down. It also highlights the Sabbat is full of gross nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is an eternal mystery to me to be honest<br /> You were very generous with the 800 years<br /> Velya at least by my math is at least 1300 years old; his Sire, Triglav was beheaded by Dracon around 700 CE (Constantinople by Night put Gesu's Embrace in 701 CE and he falls into a deep torpor; Dracon blamed the Transylvanian Tzimisce, especially Triglav and his brood and after two years of rampage he destroyed Triglav)<br /> Velya, 5th generation Children of Triglav had to be Embraced before 703 CE<br /> Why and how one of the mightiest - if not THE mightiest surviving Koldun - with almost one and a half millenia under his belt on the Path of Metamorphosis became so attached that kid is just unfathomable to me<br /> Okay, Elaine systematically destroyed her family and Velya was... enthralled by both her appearance and her evil, made the 10 years old girl his &quot;Bride&quot;<br /> This... I actually can understand<br /> Lets be generous and lets say Velya was embraced around 500 CE - the normal age for a girl to marry in that time was around 12-15, with the legal minimum often being 12. While some marriages involved girls as young as 10 or 11, particularly in elite or political situations<br /> So as a relic of a bygone era, to him this was &quot;normal&quot; - and this is where waht you wrote a bit fall apart in my eyes; Velya not did it because of any perversion or other weird or insidious thing; for a Voivode of his age it was... something <i>normal.</i><br /> What was puzzling his love twisted by their blood bond - Velya basically invented <b>Vaulderie</b>\u200b (or at least helped to refine the rite they preformed during Kupala's Night: &quot;The land and the ruler are one, and so the Transylvanian Tzimisce show their reverence for the land by sharing their blood with each other and the earth. With the assistance of mystics, participants enact an ancient rite involving the sharing of blood, A silver cup containing the vitae of all in the ceremony is passed around to be consumed and the last few drops are poured on the ground. This not only demonstrates their alliance, but it also fortifies them for the task at hand.&quot; (Transylvania by Nigh) )<br /> The Vaulderie is the foremost ritual of the Sword of Caine. <i>It ensures freedom from the blood bond</i>\u200b , <i>breaks a blood bond</i>\u200b and replaces it with a communal bond, the Vinculum\u200b<br /> So possiblity A; despite this Velya, a ~1500 years old Koldun somehow is forced to care about his &quot;Bride&quot; and tries to help her and no one among his contemporaries in the Sabbat, Lambach (okay not the best example) , Vykos, Count Vladimir Rustovich (the Shadow Lords only destroyed him in 2002, Velya met Elaine in Boston in the 1890s...) , Radu Szantovich\u200b of Bistriz or Szechenyi Jol\u00e1n, Mother of Horrors just to name a few tired to talk some sense in him....<br /> Possibility B, Velya... truly loves and cares about his &quot;bride&quot; for some reason - in this case he is truly a tragic character, but we have the same scenario of possibility A<br /> <br /> It... just makes 0 sense and it is infuriating in my eyes<br /> It not makes him a weird or an evil enemy you feel justified or want to destroy because he is a Grrr rawr evil monster of the Sabbat...<br /> ... just a sad old man who despite all of his wisdom and age just simply unable to let Elaine go (nor heard of the Children of Osiris tho' they probably would not helped him to save his &quot;Bride&quot;\u200b - a trivial problem when you have nicknames like &quot;the Flayer&quot; and &quot;the Vivisectionist&quot;, Koldun grand master, master of spirits and Auspex and bloodbonds... )<br /> He is more like an old distant relative you meet only on family gatherings and feel very uncomfortable to be around with<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T13:28:16-07:00","id":1554648,"title":"","content":"Fascinating analysis, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> <br /> <br /> I mean the reason he fell in love with her is she was a monstrous Michael Myers-esque psychopath so I don't think we can really sympathize too much.<br /> <br /> And as a Medieval historian, betrohals happened at 12 but actual marriages were supposed to wait til sixteen or so.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Because Medieval people knew that it would be less likely to kill the brides in childbirth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T21:14:50-07:00","id":1554656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554638#post1554638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest I never understood the hype surrounding Vykos</div> </div> </div> </div>Teenagers. The answer is teenagers. Most people won't really look a character beyond their <i>rule-of-cool</i> aspect, much less when those people are teenagers.<br /> <br /> Not everyone is like that and a lot of diversity applies, but as a general trend this was the reason behind Vykos' hype. In fact, most (not all, <u><b>most</b></u>) hype around the <b>Tzimisce</b> and <b>Lasombra</b> is this (in a sense it applies for the whole VtM, but that's another discussion).<br /> <br /> On Velya... I think this analysis puts too much stock on his reasoning mind.<br /> <br /> People are messy, even the most wise ones, and vampires aren't related in the game as being an exception, but the opposite.<br /> <br /> However inhuman they may seem and their desires may look, they have an all-too-human <i>pathos</i>. They're passionate and, more frequently than they like to admit, impulsive.<br /> <br /> Velya is rather ok in this regard in my book. He had a moment of pure passion and acted on it. This doesn't need logic, it doesn't even need be for the reasons he thinks it is, her evil is just a <i>post hoc </i>justification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T16:00:42-07:00","id":1554672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554656#post1554656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Teenagers. The answer is teenagers. Most people won't really look a character beyond their <i>rule-of-cool</i> aspect, much less when those people are teenagers.<br /> <br /> Not everyone is like that and a lot of diversity applies, but as a general trend this was the reason behind Vykos' hype. In fact, most (not all, <u><b>most</b></u>) hype around the <b>Tzimisce</b> and <b>Lasombra</b> is this (in a sense it applies for the whole VtM, but that's another discussion).<br /> <br /> On Velya... I think this analysis puts too much stock on his reasoning mind.<br /> <br /> People are messy, even the most wise ones, and vampires aren't related in the game as being an exception, but the opposite.<br /> <br /> However inhuman they may seem and their desires may look, they have an all-too-human <i>pathos</i>. They're passionate and, more frequently than they like to admit, impulsive.<br /> <br /> Velya is rather ok in this regard in my book. He had a moment of pure passion and acted on it. This doesn't need logic, it doesn't even need be for the reasons he thinks it is, her evil is just a <i>post hoc </i>justification.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X1HBIBXu7UY\" data-code=\"X1HBIBXu7UY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/X1HBIBXu7UY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T12:52:35-07:00","id":1554786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554258#post1554258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another couple of characters I have an issue with:<br /> <br /> <b>Khalil Ravana</b>: I think someone thought it'd be fun to have the Ravnos signature character be fun critique of the fact that everyone assumed the Clan was full of bad stereotypes by...making a character who is every awful stereotype combined. Khalil is a diablerist, liar, thief, and repulsive piece of crap without any real redeeming qualities. His sheer lack of virtues does make him stand out in the Clan Novels but not in a good way.<br /> <br /> Basically, Hesha is a priest of pure darkness and Vykos is a diabolical mastermind while Khalil is the kind of player character who pulls out a shotgun to blow up an Elder then rob their house during a quest giving session. There were some interesting ideas with the guy like him being possessed by Hazimel as well as the genuinely funny joke he did with Ramona. &quot;Hey, don't you disrespect Romani. They're not a bunch of thieves and murderers. I AM but that's just me. Really, I'm a genuine disgrace to my family.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Evil Saulot</b>: I think someone really thought revealing Saulot was an evil mastermind was one of the coolest ideas ever and never realized that it wasn't nearly as interesting as they thought. &quot;Okay, he's a bastard. Now how does that make him different from any other Antediluvian?&quot; I also felt that it was revealed in a way that I think didn't really do the necessary legwork. Revealing him as the guy who created the Baali was supposed to be, &quot;Oh, he made the worst of the worst!&quot; Except V:TM Cainite lore is based on the premise that God punished Caine by turning them into undead. You could easily read Saulot punishing the Baali founders by making them 4th generation and then going, &quot;Oh shit. That was a bad idea.&quot; Arguably, it's way more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554258#post1554258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The diablerie of Tremere was a massive fuck up as he initially planned to integrate the Tremere as a magus arm of the Clan Salubri to help exterminate the fiends as well as gain incredibly levels of magical insight. unfortunately Tremere was no patsy and by the time he'd managed to wrestle control of Tremere's body Clan Salubri had been exterminated and he'd lost centuries of time. A massive disaster for his long term plans on a number of fronts and is now scrambling to catch up as the sheer scale of spiritual threats in the 21st century is alarming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that idea.<br /> <br /> My personal headcanon is Saulot was a good guy who was put on a pedastal by Caine for seeming like Abel and then was looked to as Vampire Jesus, putting a lot of stress on him to act like an icon of good when he was mostly an ok guy not perfect. So his mistakes were him desperately trying to be what others saw him.<br /> <br /> I love the Tremere idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> For me I'm going to say Okulos in Gehenna. He is an author's hammer to kill any and all interesting plotlines with nothing to make him fun. He kills Victoria Ash, Smiling Jack, and worst he somehow kills a 4th gen with just a flare gun. It's infuriating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T20:51:27-07:00","id":1554818,"title":"","content":"Saulot's major problem is that the fandom leaned to the Grimdark side far more than the game was really intended to and couldn't accept elements that weren't awful. Ignoring that it actually makes the setting duller and less diverse.<br /> <br /> There were many things that could have been done with him that increased variety in the setting. But the developers had to put a lot of effort into just making him more likable to the wrong people (those who didn't like the character to begin with).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T21:05:32-07:00","id":1554821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554818#post1554818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saulot's major problem is that the fandom leaned to the Grimdark side far more than the game was really intended to and couldn't accept elements that weren't awful. Ignoring that it actually makes the setting duller and less diverse.<br /> <br /> There were many things that could have been done with him that increased variety in the setting. But the developers had to put a lot of effort into just making him more likable to the wrong people (those who didn't like the character to begin with).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's why I gave his Gehenna scenario a pass as he makes the sacrifice of his immortality that destroys the Antediluvians. Mind you, he's also in a clone body that apparently doesn't have a soul so that adventure has flaws.<br /> <br /> I still like it better than the Lilith one that is the 2nd most on the rails story of all V:TM modules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T21:19:16-07:00","id":1554823,"title":"","content":"I think the Least Favorite List needs an acknowledgement of &quot;Real Life Historical Persona is a Vampire.&quot;<br /> <br /> Measured from best to worst.<br /> <br /> <b>Al Capone</b> is a love him or hate him character because we know what happened to Al Capone and there's no mysterious disappearance that really allows him to live again any more than Elvis.<br /> He's also inherently silly (Al Capone is a gangster in charge of Chicago's underworld!). The thing is that if you don't MIND a little silly, he's not the worst person you could pick for a vampire if you were a Ventrue. Inherently, he's kind of a litmus test for how much you are willing to take your World of Darkness to cheese.<br /> <br /> (And inherently, the WOD is a 90s comic book like Spawn or Batman: Knightfall or the Crow--acknowledging this makes it better not worse)<br /> <br /> <b>Lous Pasteur</b> is a weird choice for a vampire. However, I've used him despite this and actually quite like the idea he is the kind of guy who would be able to crack vampirism scientifically. Not out of any vast magical knowledge but that he was the guy who knew what we needed to do with milk.<br /> <br /> Then there's <b>Rasputin</b> that is a bad joke that was never really funny in the first place. I actually enjoyed the Alan Rickman biography on the guy so seeing him used in Anastasia, The Kingsmen, Doctor Who, and Hellboy doesn't really feel all that tasteful. The guy may or may not have believed his own religious heresy but the poor bastard was murdered by people who got away with it and he's not really that fun to make fun of.<br /> <br /> <b>Saint Germaine</b> basically is one that just is kind of boring to adapt because he's been adapted many times already into vampire fiction. Hell, even in Assassins Creed V, though the time period was all wrong for that one. If you're going to adapt a guy to becoming a vampire then a guy with associations with the supernatural is probably a good idea. <b>John Dee</b> gets a pass for this as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Erich Weiss</b>: I don't like this guy for the simple fact that I actually think he'd make a much better version of the Arcanum or Technocracy. Many people wrote pulpy stories about him as an occult detective but he doesn't really work as a Tremere, let alone an Anarch Tremere.<br /> <br /> <b>The Final Reich</b>: I'm not sure what needs to be said here but weirdly, Himmelr isn't the worst so much as Goring. Putting aside the incredibly poor taste of it, actually, no let's not put aside the poor taste. It's all in poor taste but Goring is just a WEIRD choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T21:50:17-07:00","id":1554827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554821#post1554821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, he's also in a clone body that apparently doesn't have a soul so that adventure has flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily.<br /> <br /> Precisely because it's a soulless clone, it's relevance is actually up in the air, as is its actual relation (if any) to the original.<br /> <br /> So it isn't really something that had to be addressed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554823#post1554823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Least Favorite List needs an acknowledgement of &quot;Real Life Historical Persona is a Vampire.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Then there's <b>Rasputin</b> that is a bad joke that was never really funny in the first place. I actually enjoyed the Alan Rickman biography on the guy so seeing him used in Anastasia, The Kingsmen, Doctor Who, and Hellboy doesn't really feel all that tasteful. The guy may or may not have believed his own religious heresy but the poor bastard was murdered by people who got away with it and he's not really that fun to make fun of.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This one I agree so much.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the guy was just a horny plebe weirdo who was persecuted mostly for being a horny plebe weirdo the Tzar liked. Most serious allegations against him weren't just unfounded, but later evidence points to his innocence.<br /> <br /> How dare this poor to think he can be friends with the emperor? Lets kill him and vilify him for the rest of time.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T05:24:51-07:00","id":1554838,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> Is there anything that really implies that &quot;Herman Goring&quot; is the actual historical Herman Goring? Like, the dates line up, more or less, but just flipping through <i>Berlin by Night</i> seems pretty evident that he's probably just a confused Malkavian. Is there something I'm missing?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T02:47:05-07:00","id":1554912,"title":"","content":"2nd Edition's setup of the Antediluvian Set as some kind of video game final boss was terribly silly, and the thread on this board where someone put forward a theory that the clan as its known in the West was a misguided Hellenic cult that didn't know anything about ancient Egypt is headcanon to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T13:40:51-07:00","id":1554920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554912#post1554912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2nd Edition's setup of the Antediluvian Set as some kind of video game final boss was terribly silly, and the thread on this board where someone put forward a theory that the clan as its known in the West was a misguided Hellenic cult that didn't know anything about ancient Egypt is headcanon to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the people who said that it was actually the Children of Apophis and that they started worshiping Set ironically because Set killed his brother.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Mind you, I liked the idea that the Ravnos, Followers of Set, and a hypothetical Chinese Clan all were Clans that didn't have the Caine myth). Just like the Drowned are something that might be 14th, 15th, or 16th clans that we don't know about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-01-2025, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T13:44:55-07:00","id":1554921,"title":"","content":"Making Al Capone a Ventrue was a funny and at the same time a absurd idea as he was the most watched person in the United States thanks to the media and the fact his mind was heavily damaged by Sypslis and had the emotional and mental maturity of teenager when he did pass away. Not a promising choice for Lodin to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T13:48:46-07:00","id":1554922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554921#post1554921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making Al Capone a Ventrue was a funny and at the same time a absurd idea as he was the most watched person in the United States thanks to the media and the fact his mind was heavily damaged by Sypslis and had the emotional and mental maturity of teenager when he did pass away. Not a promising choice for Lodin to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a spoiler because it's a matter of historical record but the RL Lou Graham in Seattle died of syphilis.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The character can be made EXTREMELY MAD if you bring this up and denies it heavily.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T19:23:54-07:00","id":1554925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554920#post1554920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I liked the idea that the Ravnos, Followers of Set, and a hypothetical Chinese Clan all were Clans that didn't have the Caine myth). Just like the Drowned are something that might be 14th, 15th, or 16th clans that we don't know about.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, one of the reasons why it was bad for VtM to focus so much on Noddism as the main legend is that it doesn't really make a lot of sense for so many old vampires.<br /> <br /> Christianity only exists since the 1st century and only began to spread for real from Palestine by the end of the century. And the process of christianization of Europe took far more time. Rome itself wouldn't convert in numbers until the 4th century, and that was only the <i>beginning</i>, the rest of Europe was still pagan. The conversion of Europe would take several centuries, it would only be a majority religion in the continent by the 6th century (by kingdom, a hard to tell when by total number of followers), consolidate its hegemony in Western Europe by the 9th, complete Central and Northern Europe by the 12th, and Lithuania's nobility and royalty would only convert for real in a process that took from 1386 to 1389 for the capital, all the way to 1413 for the last standing territory formally pagan.<br /> <br /> So there are still <u>many</u> Elders who didn't undergo the transmutation into Methuselah that <i><b>personally</b></i> remember Europe before Christianity being so hegemonic, and a few that remember it before it started to take root for real. Many probably weren't Christians when alive. How many were actually educated into vampire society by Christian vampires? The Tremere Inner Circle were pagans themselves.<br /> <br /> Pagan legends for the origins of vampires should by all means still be around, even if as mostly discredited stories. Sure this time frame is still enough for most Elders to be Christians, but the total lack of alternative mythologies, that's way bizarre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T19:28:32-07:00","id":1554926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554925#post1554925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, one of the reasons why it was bad for VtM to focus so much on Noddism as the main legend is that it doesn't really make a lot of sense for so many old vampires.<br /> <br /> Christianity only exists since the 1st century and only began to spread for real from Palestine by the end of the century. And the process of christianization of Europe took far more time. Rome itself wouldn't convert in numbers until the 4th century, and that was only the <i>beginning</i>, the rest of Europe was still pagan. The conversion of Europe would take several centuries, it would only be a majority religion in the continent by the 6th century (by kingdom, a hard to tell when by total number of followers), consolidate its hegemony in Western Europe by the 9th, complete Central and Northern Europe by the 12th, and Lithuania's nobility and royalty would only convert for real in a process that took from 1386 to 1389 for the capital, all the way to 1413 for the last standing territory formally pagan.<br /> <br /> So there are still <u>many</u> Elders who didn't undergo the transmutation into Methuselah that <i><b>personally</b></i> remember Europe before Christianity being so hegemonic, and a few that remember it before it started to take root for real. Many probably weren't Christians when alive. How many were actually educated into vampire society by Christian vampires? The Tremere Inner Circle were pagans themselves.<br /> <br /> Pagan legends for the origins of vampires should by all means still be around, even if as mostly discredited stories. Sure this time frame is still enough for most Elders to be Christians, but the total lack of alternative mythologies, that's way bizarre.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the people pointed out how little sense it would make for the Laibon to believe in the Caine Myth with only a small portion of the continent being Christian but they ignored that Muslim Cainites would also believe in the Caine Myth.<br /> <br /> Presumably also Judaic.<br /> <br /> But that's if the Myth is meant to be CORRECT. Obviously, in a world where it isn't, the Caine Myth would just be one of many legends for these various Abrhamic religions (let alone all the others). Even so, I think the game could have gone much further than the Followers of Set and Ravnos having their own myths (and that is obviously not true thanks to the Gehenna supplements).<br /> <br /> Still, that's probably an insoluable problem as once you establish a mythology for something you either have to stick with it or make it completely opaque forever. Mind you, the issue is tying vampires to a RL mythology versus a fictional backstory like Akasha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-01-2025, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T19:55:28-07:00","id":1554930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554926#post1554926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the people pointed out how little sense it would make for the Laibon to believe in the Caine Myth with only a small portion of the continent being Christian but they ignored that Muslim Cainites would also believe in the Caine Myth.<br /> <br /> Presumably also Judaic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Laibon are mostly for Subsaharan Africa, and there weren't many of <i>any</i> &quot;Abrahamic&quot; faiths until very recently. Muslim and Jew Cainites in Africa would have this relevance only in the Maghreb, which is historically more linked to Europe through the Mediterranean, anyway. Even then it doesn't change much of what I said, before the 2nd century the myth of Caine would be virtually non-existent outside Palestine, being relegated to Jew vampires.<br /> <br /> Now, is it an unsolvable problem? I'm not so sure. While it's really strong in the culture of the player base, Noddism has never been officially correct. And by their own nature, <i>Gehenna</i> scenarios don't solve anything, either. Even now all it takes for new myths to become a thing is for the authors to work on it. Certainly it isn't an <i>easy</i> task due to the long history of neglect, but is still doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T12:24:48-08:00","id":1554978,"title":"","content":"This is why I prefer the Followers of Set version of how they came to be over the Caine origin.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of my favorite short stories involved Ibrham and his fellow Ashira clan mates frustration with the most ancient members of the clan attitude towards their religious war.<br /> <br /> I mean why would Montono, and the rest care for it when they saw their people and beliefs die out? They couldn't wrap there heads around the disinterest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T13:05:46-08:00","id":1554979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1554978#post1554978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I prefer the Followers of Set version of how they came to be over the Caine origin.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of my favorite short stories involved Ibrham and his fellow Ashira clan mates frustration with the most ancient members of the clan attitude towards their religious war.<br /> <br /> I mean why would Montono, and the rest care for it when they saw their people and beliefs die out? They couldn't wrap there heads around the disinterest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, there's the &quot;non-religious&quot; Caine myth.<br /> <br /> Which is that the myth of Caine is true in the world of darkness but has absolutely nothing specifically to do with Abrahamic religion other than it was recorded by them. Which is sort of Menele and Helena being people who have had a version of their life stories recorded by Homer even though it clearly isn't the accurate story.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of a cop out but it is the kind of thing a Noddist scholar might speculate on. Similarly, Set might well be the first vampire and cursed for killing Osiris but people adapted that legend into the Caine one. I also had a Babylonian version of the legend.<br /> <br /> The basics of the story were the same: &quot;One original undead, spreads to 3, spreads to 13, curses and floods.&quot; but the gods involved changed by culture because it's meant to be a historical event that was interpreted across human history.<br /> <br /> In one of my games, we also made it so that Caine was actually a Revenant raised by Lilith (A proto-Verbena) and learned how to spread his curse and it's just the immense AGE of the Antediluvian vampires versus any actual superpower inherent to the 1st generation. God was never involved, at least in terms of the Curses and origins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T00:35:25-08:00","id":1555007,"title":"","content":"Just keep in mind that flood myths are not universal.<br /> <br /> The biblical flood has direct parallels nearby because it's of Mesopotamian origins. It's probably related to a real but localized flood.<br /> <br /> Other cultures have flood myths, but most don't. Even those who have, have considerably distinct myths as they're drawn from different events and legends.<br /> <br /> But it may be a common element for vampires <b>if</b> you assume their origins in Mesopotamia or near it, and only after the flood they started to spread out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T01:16:13-08:00","id":1555011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1555007#post1555007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just keep in mind that flood myths are not universal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to differ<br /> There are more than 400 legends and myths of a worldwide deluge. Many of these show remarkable similarities like a certain family being forewarned and spared the destruction, the flood having been due to the wickedness of man or at least widespread evil, a bird being sent out from the ark to scout for dry land and so on<br /> And every continent have their own... from Australia's Kurnai people to East Africa's Masai legends to Mexico's Codex Chimalpopoca, the Hawaiian legend of Nu-u, the Great Flood of Gun-Yu in China, several Indian scripts and a tons of native american legends; Brazil has several flood myths, notably the one from the Tupi-Guarani People where the god Tup\u00e3 sends a great flood to cleanse the earth because of humanity's negligence...\u200b<br /> \u200bFrom six continents and the islands of the sea; hundreds of such legends are known<br /> I would say if one thing this one is pretty universal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T01:47:27-08:00","id":1555013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554145-everyone-s-least-favorite-vtm-character?p=1555011#post1555011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say if one thing this one is pretty universal</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you want to focus on the similarities and not on what I actually said.<br /> <br /> Languages alone are more than 6 thousands around the world right now, and we never had so few of them in recorded history.<br /> <br /> And the differences between those legends are far more relevant than their similarities, which are usually on very superficial and obvious aspects.<br /> <br /> The theme of humanity becoming unworthy and the gods punishing them, sometimes with the exception of a virtuous individual/family who is spared, is itself pretty common and link to many, many, many sorts of catastrophes. Fires, wars, plagues, droughts, meteors, predators, swarms, monsters, everything and anything. Floods are just a subclass on a very broad class of legends, with some cultures having several of those.<br /> <br /> So no, this is far from universal, very far. First in the sense that while there are cultures with such myths in every inhabited continent, in none of those they are all cultures. Quite the opposite, most cultures have no such myths. Second in the sense that those legends are quite different from each other past very, very broad strokes that aren't really specific to flood myths to begin with.<br /> <br /> We have a legend of &quot;universal flood myths&quot; because we have a history of Christian apologists and Christian Archaeologists that purposefully built a corpus of arguments in favor of a &quot;global flood event&quot; that would have been recorded by all cultures. And it was briefly reinforced by the many similarities between the biblical flood and the Epic of Gilgamesh.<br /> <br /> Recently, though, we confirmed that the similarities between the biblical and the Mesopotamian floods are due to it being the same myth. The Hebrews learned it in Babylon and then elaborated a version/response where it happens but their god is more powerful. Originally a reader of the story of Noah would also know the Babylonian version and it would have some additional layers of meaning because of that.<br /> <br /> Other than that, no, the flood myths of other cultures have nothing besides the obvious to do with the biblical flood, they refer to other events, and even if perceived by their culture as global (another thing that's fairly common in mythology, as every culture is the center of the world in their myths), they would have happened in different times and with different caracteristics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}